Variable Refrigerant Flow (VRF) systems are advanced HVAC solutions that circulate refrigerant as the cooling and heating medium through a network of indoor units connected to a single outdoor unit equipped with variable speed compressors. This architecture enables precise temperature control, energy savings of up to 30 40% compared with conventional systems, and flexible zoning for commercial and high rise buildings.
